#: inc/cpcff_connector_api.inc.php:441
msgid "Create WordPress form via CFF plugin"
msgstr ""

#: inc/cpcff_connector_api.inc.php:443
msgid ""
"Creates a new form inside the user's WordPress site using the Calculated "
"Fields Form plugin. Call this when the user asks to create a new form for "
"their site: it returns the prompt template, the endpoint URL where the agent "
"POSTs the generated structure, and the usage instructions. The endpoint "
"validates the structure against js/schema.min.json and renders a preview for "
"admin confirmation before saving. Do NOT generate a standalone HTML file "
"instead — this tool is the canonical way to create a form inside the "
"WordPress site."
msgstr ""

#: inc/cpcff_connector_api.inc.php:501
msgid "Issue CFF form preview URL"
msgstr ""

#: inc/cpcff_connector_api.inc.php:503
msgid ""
"Stores the agent-generated form structure in a transient and returns a short "
"preview URL with a one-time token. The user opens the URL in their own "
"browser (already authenticated to WordPress via cookies) to see the preview "
"and click \"Use this form\" to confirm and save. The structure is sent as "
"input; the returned preview_url is short (token-based) and clickable."
msgstr ""

#: inc/cpcff_connector_api.inc.php:517
msgid ""
"JSON-encoded [fields_array, settings_array] structure produced by the agent."
msgstr ""

#: inc/cpcff_connector_api.inc.php:521
msgid "Display name the admin will see on the preview page."
msgstr ""

#: inc/cpcff_connector_api.inc.php:533
